% Daml patterns: coin issuance by an issuer's invitation (propose and accept)
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Daml project, written by the Daml translator
% from its source: each template a fluent keyed by the contract id, each create and choice an action,
% who may do what integrity constraints. The source is kept in sources/ (File > Show the Original in the
% Logical English editor, View > The original this was converted from in the LPS2 IDE).
% The ids of the contracts a command creates are places of its action: the ledger assigns them, a scenario names them.
% Who may do what, as one permission per command: the legal view
% (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program in the Logical English editor, View > Legal view in the LPS2 IDE).
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from a program of another
% system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
% implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or fit for a
% particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against its source
% before relying on it. It is not legal, tax, insurance, financial or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 8.

the actions are:
    *a party* creates the coin master *a coin master* with issuer *an issuer*; known as create_coin_master.
    *a party* creates the coin issue proposal *a coin issue proposal* with coin agreement issuer *a coin agreement issuer* and coin agreement owner *a coin agreement owner*; known as create_coin_issue_proposal.
    *a party* creates the coin issue agreement *a coin issue agreement* with issuer *an issuer* and owner *an owner*; known as create_coin_issue_agreement.
    *a party* creates the coin *a coin* with owner *an owner*, issuer *an issuer*, amount *an amount* and delegates party list *a delegates party list*; known as create_coin.
    *a party* creates the locked coin *a locked coin* with coin owner *a coin owner*, coin issuer *a coin issuer*, coin amount *a coin amount*, coin delegates party list *a coin delegates party list*, maturity *a maturity* and locker *a locker*; known as create_locked_coin.
    *a party* creates the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal* with coin owner *a coin owner*, coin issuer *a coin issuer*, coin amount *a coin amount*, coin delegates party list *a coin delegates party list* and new owner *a new owner*; known as create_transfer_proposal.
    *a party* archives the coin master *a coin master*; known as archive_coin_master.
    *a party* archives the coin issue proposal *a coin issue proposal*; known as archive_coin_issue_proposal.
    *a party* archives the coin issue agreement *a coin issue agreement*; known as archive_coin_issue_agreement.
    *a party* archives the coin *a coin*; known as archive_coin.
    *a party* archives the locked coin *a locked coin*; known as archive_locked_coin.
    *a party* archives the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal*; known as archive_transfer_proposal.
    *a party* exercises invite on the coin master *a coin master* with owner *an owner* creating *a coin issue proposal*; known as invite.
    *a party* exercises accept coin proposal on the coin issue proposal *a coin issue proposal* creating *a coin issue agreement*; known as accept_coin_proposal.
    *a party* exercises issue on the coin issue agreement *a coin issue agreement* with amount *an amount* creating *a coin*; known as issue.
    *a party* exercises transfer on the coin *a coin* with new owner *a new owner* creating *a transfer proposal*; known as transfer.
    *a party* exercises lock on the coin *a coin* with maturity *a maturity* and locker *a locker* creating *a locked coin*; known as lock.
    *a party* exercises archives on the coin *a coin*; known as archives.
    *a party* exercises unlock on the locked coin *a locked coin* creating *a coin*; known as unlock.
    *a party* exercises withdraw proposal on the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal* creating *a coin*; known as withdraw_proposal.
    *a party* exercises accept transfer on the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal* creating *a coin*; known as accept_transfer.
    *a party* exercises reject transfer on the transfer proposal *a transfer proposal*; known as reject_transfer.

the fluents are:
    *a coin master* is a coin master with issuer *an issuer*; known as coin_master.
    *a coin issue proposal* is a coin issue proposal with coin agreement issuer *a coin agreement issuer* and coin agreement owner *a coin agreement owner*; known as coin_issue_proposal.
    *a coin issue agreement* is a coin issue agreement with issuer *an issuer* and owner *an owner*; known as coin_issue_agreement.
    *a coin* is a coin with owner *an owner*, issuer *an issuer*, amount *an amount* and delegates party list *a delegates party list*; known as coin.
    *a locked coin* is a locked coin with coin owner *a coin owner*, coin issuer *a coin issuer*, coin amount *a coin amount*, coin delegates party list *a coin delegates party list*, maturity *a maturity* and locker *a locker*; known as locked_coin.
    *a transfer proposal* is a transfer proposal with coin owner *a coin owner*, coin issuer *a coin issuer*, coin amount *a coin amount*, coin delegates party list *a coin delegates party list* and new owner *a new owner*; known as transfer_proposal.

the knowledge base coin_issuance includes:

the text of "the source daml/CoinIssuance.daml" is at "sources/daml/CoinIssuance.daml".

the text of "the source daml/Utilities.daml" is at "sources/daml/Utilities.daml".

% CoinMaster: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the coin master a coin master with issuer an issuer
then the coin master is a coin master with issuer the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the coin master a coin master with issuer an issuer
    and the party is different from the issuer.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the coin master a coin master with issuer an issuer
    and the coin master is a coin master with issuer a second issuer.

