% Daml (the script run on a Canton sandbox) ends with these active contracts (their payloads;
% the ids are the ledger's):
%   - coin_master(bank)
%   - coin_issue_agreement(bank,me)
%   - transfer_proposal(you,bank,100.0,[],me)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_daml.pl.
scenario coin_issuance is:
    % the Daml Script coinIssuance
    bank creates the coin master master_id with issuer bank from 1 to 2.
    bank exercises invite on the coin master master_id with owner me creating coin_agm_prop from 2 to 3.
    me exercises accept coin proposal on the coin issue proposal coin_agm_prop creating coin_agm_id from 3 to 4.
    bank exercises issue on the coin issue agreement coin_agm_id with amount 100.0 creating coin_id from 4 to 5.
    me exercises transfer on the coin coin_id with new owner you creating coin_transfer_prop_id from 5 to 6.
    you exercises accept transfer on the transfer proposal coin_transfer_prop_id creating coin_id from 6 to 7.

